    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16312" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκωλι-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hop on greased wineskins at the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσκώλια,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				1129
			</span></i> (cf. Sch.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>hop on one leg,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκωλιάζειν ῥᾷον ἐπὶ τοῖς
					ἀριστεροῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>IA</u>
					705b33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				3.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.621f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.106
			</span></i>; also, <i>jump up and down with legs held together,</i>
				Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				3p.689D.
			</span></i> (Signf. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i> may be original and the connexion with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκός</span> due to popular etymology.)</div>
